  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Urgent Humanitarian Needs of Conflict-Affected Populations in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over a year into the full-scale Russia-Ukraine war, military operations persist, most acutely in eastern and southern Ukraine. The crisis precipitated large-scale displacement, both within Ukraine and across borders. This project seeks to improve the living conditions of the most vulnerable conflict-affected populations through various interventions. This includes: 1) improved living conditions of vulnerable, conflict-affected populations through essential non-food items (NFIs) and access to dignified shelter; 2)  war-affected populations have better access to quality water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services; 3) war-affected populations have flexible means to meet their basic needs; 4) improved protection and psychosocial well-being of vulnerable war-affected populations; and 5) improved capacity of stakeholders to deliver quality, targeted humanitarian support.</narrative>
  </description>
